@node Common invoking options, Invoking zebra, zebra, zebra
@comment  node-name,  next,  previous,  up
@section Common invoking options

These options are common to all Zebra daemons.

@table @samp

@item -d
@itemx --daemon
Runs in daemon mode.

@item -f @var{file}
@itemx --config_file=@var{file}
Set configuration file name.

@item -l
@itemx --log_mode
Set verbose log mode flag.

@item -P @var{port}
@itemx --vty_port=@var{port}
Set vty's port number.

@item -v
@itemx --version
Print program version.

@item -h
@itemx --help
Display this help and exit.

@end table

@node Invoking zebra, Interface, Common invoking options, zebra
@comment  node-name,  next,  previous,  up
@section Invoking zebra

Besides common invoking options (@pxref{Common invoking options}). Below
is @code{zebra} specific invoking options.

@table @samp
@item -b
@itemx --batch
Runs in batch mode.  @code{zebra} parse configuration file and terminate
immediately.

@item -k
@itemx --keep_kernel
When zebra starts up, don't delete old self inserted route.

@item -r
@itemx --retain
When program terminates, retain added route by zebra.

@end table

